<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.carr.nightly-record-layer</string>

  <!-- THE SAME SCRIPT THE SCHEDULED TASK RUNS (rule a8c55a47: a manual path and
       an automated path that do the same job must be the same code). This agent
       adds a second RUNNER, never a second implementation. bin/nightly.sh
       refuses a second completed run in the same day, so whichever fires first
       wins and the other exits 0 with a SKIP line in out/nightly.log.

       WHY IT EXISTS. The Claude Code scheduled task fires at 02:05 only when
       the app is open in a logged-in session. On 2026-08-09 the Mac booted at
       02:16 — after the window, still at the login screen — so the chain did
       not run until Joe logged in at 06:59, and the health check reported a
       5.0h schedule drift. `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 01:55:00`
       was ALREADY set and could not fix it: powering a Mac on is not the same
       as having a session to run in.

       WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT FIX. It removes the dependency on the Claude
       Code app being open, which is the ordinary failure: Mac asleep, Joe still
       logged in, wakepoweron brings it up at 01:55, launchd fires at 02:05. It
       does NOT fix a cold boot with nobody logged in — a LaunchAgent has no
       session then either, and the only thing that would is a LaunchDaemon in
       /Library/LaunchDaemons, which needs sudo. The scheduled task remains as
       the fallback that catches those mornings on wake. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/nightly.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!-- 02:05 daily, matching the scheduled task's cron `0 2 * * *` plus its
       jitter. SEVEN DAYS: the record layer has no weekend stand-down — the
       generated files must be true whenever either partner opens them, and
       every Cowork and phone session reads them. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>2</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>5</integer></dict>
  </array>

  <!-- Catch up if the machine was off at 02:05 rather than skipping the day. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>{{REPO}}/out/nightly-launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>{{REPO}}/out/nightly-launchd.log</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
